   "materials": [{"title": "Cells notes (slides)", "url": "https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/abc/edit", "kind": "slides", "text": "Cell theory: 1) All living things are made of cells. 2) Cells are the basic unit of life. 3) All cells come from existing cells.\nOrganelles: nucleus (control center, holds DNA), mitochondria (powerhouse, makes ATP), ribosome (makes proteins), cell membrane (controls what enters/leaves), cell wall (plants only, support), chloroplast (plants only, photosynthesis), vacuole (storage; large in plants).\nPlant vs animal: plants have cell wall, chloroplasts, one large vacuole. Animals have small vacuoles, no wall, no chloroplasts."}]},
